    "limits": [
      "capabilities are bound in-process to the declared targets; what stops a handler reaching around them is the lint, a discipline, until the opt-in sandbox (PT6.5, S134, S152)",
      "the store is SQLite only; Postgres is not built (S135)",
      "installed packages are hashed, not linted: a package's own I/O is stopped only by the opt-in sandbox (S154)",
      "a call's cost is its provider's usage report at the certified prices (K15): a call whose provider gave no answer reports no usage and its reservation is released, so what a provider bills for such a call is not counted; a usage report that is not whole token counts fails the call; a reservation covers the token limit at the highest price, which a call over its input tokens may exceed, recorded as an overrun"
    ],
